---
# ESP-IDF and Matter glue: the apps and the ESP-only components under
# apps/components. The code here talks to C APIs and ESP-IDF/esp-matter
# macros, so a few checks have no call-site fix. They stay on for the
# portable components (firmware/components) and the host tests.
#
#   hicpp-signed-bitwise
#       ESP_LOGx expands to `(level) | ESP_LOG_CONFIGS_DEFAULT` on signed
#       enums, so it fires on every log call (and on the NimBLE flag macros).
#   bugprone-macro-parentheses
#       esp-matter builds define CHIP_ADDRESS_RESOLVE_IMPL_INCLUDE_HEADER=<...>
#       on the command line; the finding has no source location (so no
#       NOLINT) and an include target cannot be parenthesised. The glue's own
#       few macros are simple (COUNT_OF, PIN_ARG).
# C++ only (the hub's Matter shim; C files never trigger these):
#   cppcoreguidelines-pro-type-vararg, hicpp-vararg
#       ESP_LOGx and printf are the platform's logging and console output.
#   cppcoreguidelines-pro-type-union-access
#       The interface types are C tagged unions (lp_msg_t, ChipDeviceEvent,
#       esp_matter_attr_val_t), and ESP_LOGx expands to a union access.
#   cppcoreguidelines-pro-bounds-pointer-arithmetic,
#   cppcoreguidelines-pro-bounds-array-to-pointer-decay, hicpp-no-array-decay
#       Console handlers get argv as char **, and the C APIs take char * plus
#       a size; there is no std::span on this side of the boundary.
InheritParentConfig: true
Checks: >
  -hicpp-signed-bitwise,
  -bugprone-macro-parentheses,
  -cppcoreguidelines-pro-type-vararg,
  -hicpp-vararg,
  -cppcoreguidelines-pro-type-union-access,
  -cppcoreguidelines-pro-bounds-pointer-arithmetic,
  -cppcoreguidelines-pro-bounds-array-to-pointer-decay,
  -hicpp-no-array-decay,
...
